{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg9wyyqJGtQ82S9LesSfa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The path-separator check now runs on every `--and` pattern as well as the main pattern. Before, `fd foo --and one/two` quietly returned nothing; now it errors with the same message, naming the pattern that has the separator.\n\n- **`src/main.rs`:** I split the per-pattern check into `ensure_pattern_is_not_a_path(pattern)`. `ensure_search_pattern_is_not_a_path` still skips the check under `--full-path`, then runs it on the main pattern and on each `--and` pattern.\n- **`tests/tests.rs`:** I added a case for `--and one/two` to `test_pattern_with_forward_slash_is_rejected`.\n\nThe two forward-slash tests pass and clippy reports nothing. I didn't run the full test suite, and I didn't build or test on Windows, where the extra `\\` check also now applies to `--and` patterns. Nothing is committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":388,"cache_read_input_tokens":36068,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":388,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b2865558-2bb5-4984-8213-23d32bda2372","uuid":"bc9f8ff9-5547-4fb1-ba35-9c8c322bad73","timestamp":"2026-10-18T15:35:44.749Z","request_id":"req_011Cg9wyyWTqsedHR1KARPPx"}
